Z||000000||Smokey||02-26-2000||01:28 AM||||I got offered a job up-state as a manager of a garage and I need a reliable car now. My Fiero isn't that bad...it looks real nice, interior is in good condition..no cracks in the dash or anything just the good ole rip in the driver seat along the side. It just has a habit of running like crap on me every now and then. Nothing real big goes wrong...just little stuff all the time. Like a sensor here, an alternator there, ya know..stuff like that, it does have 172,000 miles on it so i guess its expected. Anyway, I'm trading it even up for an RX7, only has 90,000 miles, 5 speed, very reliable, and she'll take it sideways through 3 gears :-) Once I get up to the garage and get settled down with some money rolling in, it's off for a GT hunt....||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||02-26-2000||10:11 AM||||who says RX-7's are "very reliable"?  the owner?<P>i owned one (a '91), and yes it was good transportation. however it would flood on me once every month and a half to two.  what a *****  to get started when it floods.  i would often have to take the plugs out for a day, let the rotor dry out then put new plugs back in!  <P>be carefull!!||||reg||1
