Z||000003||Smokey||02-26-2000||11:17 PM||||bhooper, i can tell you why your RX would flood. Many RX7's have "starting problems" when you start the car and move it to another spot without letting the engine reach normal operating temperature...not all the time but it is very common that the engine will be flooded next time you start it. It doesn't matter if you let it sit for a year....It will be flooded next time you start it. It's a problem with the computer in the RX's that causes this, the only way to completely avoid it is to let the car reach normal temperature before u shut it off.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||02-27-2000||09:28 AM||||that sounds reasonable, except that many times it happened was the morning after i drove home from work.  and believe me the car would get to normal operating temp on the drive home.  all i know is it was a real pain to deal with!  very imbarasing at times!||||reg||1
